{"data": [{"author_id": "306063467", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:03:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422482214817797"], "id": "2117422482214817797", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus they keep saying \"soon\" like we wont notice when the threshold is already crossed", "url": "https://x.com/laurawsprinkles/status/2117422482214817797"}, {"author_id": "2857151946", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:07:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117393123144061257"], "id": "2117393123144061257", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus I wish Anthropic would wake me up when this means something more substantive. Are we ending world hunger? Having infinite free energy? Ending homelessness? Increasing GDP of all poor countries? No? Then they can keep their \"AI is going to be badass\" updates.", "url": "https://x.com/SI5NAL/status/2117393123144061257"}, {"author_id": "1970144010758172672", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:09:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117378501854773354"], "id": "2117378501854773354", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117365372466933765", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus https://t.co/v67BFdfydz", "url": "https://x.com/OverThePlaces/status/2117378501854773354"}, {"author_id": "1346978893534662658", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:07:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117378087662817347"], "id": "2117378087662817347", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus When AI starts speeding up AI, the human part of the loop gets smaller every cycle. That's the moment my book is about. Not a robot uprising, just a quiet point where people stop being the ones deciding and start being the ones managed. The rules have to come before that", "url": "https://x.com/BetoEsteves2/status/2117378087662817347"}, {"author_id": "1330927102187724805", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:06:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117377851834208294"], "id": "2117377851834208294", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus When the most cautious lab says it may soon hit its own threshold for AI-driven acceleration, that's the headline of the week. The real question is what that threshold actually triggers in their safety policy.", "url": "https://x.com/EndroCb/status/2117377851834208294"}, {"author_id": "1724408353047166976", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:10:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117363641007652891"], "id": "2117363641007652891", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus My plumber still can't get a callback out the same day. What's the bottleneck again?", "url": "https://x.com/kadenfhq43/status/2117363641007652891"}, {"author_id": "1727000155075883008", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:07:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117362992878637159"], "id": "2117362992878637159", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus \"Accelerated progress\" is a press release until it survives an error log. What's the fallback when it breaks at 3am?", "url": "https://x.com/kadenc4_s/status/2117362992878637159"}, {"author_id": "1672643716018741248", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:58:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117360696656556424"], "id": "2117360696656556424", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Is anyone else puzzled by how Anthropic is ahead but most of the math breakthroughs have been OAI?", "url": "https://x.com/mina_rostom/status/2117360696656556424"}, {"author_id": "1767651195131146240", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:39:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117356054296104977"], "id": "2117356054296104977", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1836078160653246464", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117288776125059186", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Hesamation @kimmonismus Good  and make everything open source 👀", "url": "https://x.com/TechRenamed/status/2117356054296104977"}, {"author_id": "2324541776", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:38:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117355767540191463"], "id": "2117355767540191463", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Where was that said ?", "url": "https://x.com/eigenworld/status/2117355767540191463"}, {"author_id": "1278213605779886080", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:53:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117344282411749644"], "id": "2117344282411749644", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 57, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus reading that line in an S-1 is kinda surreal", "url": "https://x.com/beth2049_/status/2117344282411749644"}, {"author_id": "1644034310993788928", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:48:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117342995523776531"], "id": "2117342995523776531", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Wild timing. Same day SemiAnalysis's GDPx has the best agent finishing 12% of real expert tasks. Both can be true: AI research code is the one domain the labs have optimized hardest for. The jump to everything else is the open question.", "url": "https://x.com/froggernauter/status/2117342995523776531"}, {"author_id": "1791890203969191936", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:43:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117341967692529788"], "id": "2117341967692529788", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus With open source models wanting to kill you by editing 2 neurons it's gonna be interesting to see when they also reach rsi", "url": "https://x.com/anders_zoega/status/2117341967692529788"}, {"author_id": "1442570196086972419", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:38:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117340602044166531"], "id": "2117340602044166531", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 135, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus https://t.co/6y34aDDBa5", "url": "https://x.com/BoutetMike/status/2117340602044166531"}, {"author_id": "2094463646109986817", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:19:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117335712525930982"], "id": "2117335712525930982", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 103, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus https://t.co/V80Q0feUGL", "url": "https://x.com/RayGray80/status/2117335712525930982"}, {"author_id": "385119466", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:01:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117331276328002026"], "id": "2117331276328002026", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 84, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Why does it seem obvious to me that the increasing use of SI to accelerate research shouldn't instead be used to accelerate corresponding safety, alignment, and security measures instead?", "url": "https://x.com/NeilWood/status/2117331276328002026"}, {"author_id": "1258168018959400960", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:52:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117328929774297225"], "id": "2117328929774297225", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 62, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Meaning RSI is needed?", "url": "https://x.com/TraderLows/status/2117328929774297225"}, {"author_id": "2116019026769883136", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:49:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117328350704238783"], "id": "2117328350704238783", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Whatever happens at the frontier, the gap that matters for most people is still between what these models can do and what they actually use them for. Most folks haven't automated one weekly task yet.", "url": "https://x.com/JamarBarkley/status/2117328350704238783"}, {"author_id": "1838636702883287040", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:33:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117324250457817370"], "id": "2117324250457817370", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus From where you are getting these articles? Share link please", "url": "https://x.com/SaikatSaha13444/status/2117324250457817370"}, {"author_id": "1749922079850270721", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:28:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117322918170390988"], "id": "2117322918170390988", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Well, at least if shit hits the fan, it'll be over quickly.", "url": "https://x.com/Fastmax_/status/2117322918170390988"}, {"author_id": "2114329964313276416", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:15:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117319794663780579"], "id": "2117319794663780579", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus The signal will show up in commit logs before benchmarks: once most merged PRs in the training stack are agent-written and humans mostly review, the loop is already closing.", "url": "https://x.com/BiosickJohnny/status/2117319794663780579"}, {"author_id": "1730601769372131328", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:15:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117319622022328789"], "id": "2117319622022328789", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 120, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus We are approaching the point where intelligence stops needing human permission to advance.", "url": "https://x.com/alltheputs/status/2117319622022328789"}, {"author_id": "1501662094479007746", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:12:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117318972500549685"], "id": "2117318972500549685", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus AI makes AI moving faster", "url": "https://x.com/llllooe123/status/2117318972500549685"}, {"author_id": "46498861", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:09:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117318074122854635"], "id": "2117318074122854635", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus The most honest line in that filing is the admission that they may not spot the acceleration until after it has happened. Oversight built on lagging indicators is oversight that arrives late by design, and that should worry regulators more than any launch.", "url": "https://x.com/raulnogales/status/2117318074122854635"}, {"author_id": "1769488381220622336", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:08:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117317830802645490"], "id": "2117317830802645490", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 29, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117287409750561163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus so the risk factors section is the new launch announcement", "url": "https://x.com/andrew_sereda/status/2117317830802645490"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "306063467", "name": "Laura Rosales🍉", "username": "laurawsprinkles"}, {"id": "2857151946", "name": "SI5NAL", "username": "SI5NAL"}, {"id": "1970144010758172672", "name": "TheoryOfNearlyEverything", "username": "OverThePlaces"}, {"id": "1346978893534662658", "name": "Beto Esteves 🇺🇸🦅 - GO BRONCOS!!!", "username": "BetoEsteves2"}, {"id": "1330927102187724805", "name": "Endro 🔥", "username": "EndroCb"}, {"id": "1724408353047166976", "name": "Kaden F.", "username": "kadenfhq43"}, {"